<h2>The Strengths of Skills</h2>
<p>Usually a product's characteristics are a list of several features built separately. Yet the strengths of skills <strong>all derive from the single idea of the "skill"</strong>. So once you understand the concept, the characteristics connect naturally.</p>

<div class="tbl-wrap">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Strength</th><th>What it means</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Reusability</strong></td><td>Build it once and productivity rises a lot even if you never share it and just use it many times yourself.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Packaging repetitive work</strong></td><td>Turn work you always do the same way into a skill and handle it easily and consistently every time.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Progressive loading</strong></td><td>Loads only when needed, reducing context waste (the core principle, in a separate document).</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Scripts and resources included</strong></td><td>Layer in proven existing scripts as they are, making probabilistic results <strong>deterministic</strong>.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Composite workflows</strong></td><td>Several skills can be loaded at once and combined (fused).</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Platform compatibility</strong></td><td>Usable in Claude AI, API, Code, and Cowork (environments and permissions differ a little). Partly usable in Codex and Antigravity as well.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Packaging expertise and organizational knowledge</strong></td><td>Standardize by capturing tone and manner, review checklists, quality standards, and the like in a skill.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<h3>Proven scripts as they are</h3>
<p>Skills turn complaints like "what the AI writes differs every time, so I can't use it" and "there are hallucinations" into <strong>deterministic results that run inside the script I provided</strong>. If you layer a proven script you have used for years (for example, a field's traditional analysis script) into a skill, you can put it to use reliably without hallucination.</p>

<div class="note">
    <span class="nh">The value it gives an organization</span>
    It carries great significance that the outputs coming out of our institution can be produced <strong>to a set quality standard</strong>. Package domain expertise and organizational knowledge into a skill, and no matter who makes it, the result is consistent &mdash; "as if one person wrote it".
</div>
